  <data name="SignedSaveWarningTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Este documento tiene una firma digital</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481, #602: Save's confirmation before overwriting a signed original (ordinary/approval signature). Says "digital signature", not just "signed", so it cannot be read as "you have signed this" in a session where the user also placed a signature from the library</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignedSaveWarningBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Si guardas sobre este documento, se invalidará su firma digital. Guarda una copia para conservar intacto el original firmado.</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="CertifiedSaveWarningTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Este documento está certificado contra cambios</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481, #602: shown instead of SignedSaveWarningTitle when the signature carries a /DocMDP certification — measured as the common case, not the rare one, on real signed documents. The title states the certification, which nothing in the Signatures feature claims; the body names the digital signature</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="CertifiedSaveWarningBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La firma digital de este documento lo certifica: su autor declaró que no debe modificarse en absoluto. Si guardas sobre él, esa firma quedará inválida. Guarda una copia para conservar intacto el original firmado.</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SaveACopyButton" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Guardar una copia</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481: the signed-document save warning's primary, default action</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="OverwriteSignedButton" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sobrescribir el original</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481: the signed-document save warning's deliberate, secondary action</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignatureNotCarriedNotice" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>La copia lleva la firma digital del original, y ya no es válida.</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #476, #481, #602, #576: said once, quietly, after Save a copy that kept the signature. It used to say the signature "doesn't carry over to this copy", which #576 measured as untrue on every platform that still said it — the signature dictionary does carry over (FPDF_SaveAsCopy re-serialises it), and the copy reports as signed when it is reopened; only its validity does not carry over</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignedSaveRemoveSignature" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Quitar también la firma, que ya no será válida</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #576: the tick added to this same warning rather than a fourth button — a button would be a different destination competing with the two already there, while a tick modifies the destination already chosen. Ticked by default: by the time this box matters the save has already ended the signature, so the tick chooses between a file that admits it is unsigned and a file that goes on claiming a signature it cannot support</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignedSaveRemoveOffer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Si se deja, viaja con el archivo guardado y sigue afirmando que describe un archivo que ya no describe, de modo que MegaPDF y otros lectores indican que ese archivo está firmado. El documento que abriste no cambia en ningún caso: esto solo afecta al archivo que se escribe. Y una firma digital indica que un archivo no ha cambiado desde que se firmó: nunca ha impedido que alguien abra este documento, así que un archivo guardado sin ella pueden leerlo exactamente las mismas personas.</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #576: what the tick means. Three things it must keep saying — the original file is untouched, the choice reaches only the file being written, and a digital signature is not encryption and never was. No "encrypt", "password", "protect", "secure", "lock" or "unlock" anywhere near it: those belong to the password feature</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SignatureRemovedNotice" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Guardado sin la firma digital del documento. El documento que abriste no ha cambiado.</value>
    <comment>ES-REVIEW #724 — new, not yet read by the reviewer. #576: said once, quietly, after a save that removed the signature — either Save a copy or Overwrite the original, whichever the tick applied to</comment>
  </data>

